<article class="env-lemma" id="02W9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02W9">Lemma <span data-tag="02W9">65.3.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme contained in $\mathit{Sch}_{fppf}$ and let $X$, $Y$ be objects of $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  h_ f : h_ X \longrightarrow h_ Y  \]
</div>
  <p> is a representable transformation of functors. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is formal and relies only on the fact that the category $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$ has fibre products. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>